      "a11y": "Document-level tab strip; you own the .df-tab-panel[data-tab-panel] sections and toggle .active.",
      "example": "<druid-tabs active=\"home\">\n  <druid-tab panel=\"home\">Home</druid-tab>\n  <druid-tab panel=\"logs\">Logs</druid-tab>\n</druid-tabs>\n<section class=\"df-tab-panel active\" data-tab-panel=\"home\">…</section>",
      "gotchas": [
        "The strip scrolls horizontally inside itself when the tabs do not fit, so it never widens the page on a narrow viewport — in the navbar or placed in content alike."
